From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: match TimeKeep's current application UID

Origin: Local ThinkSmart View port
Source: https://github.com/LineageOS/android_hardware_sony_timekeep
License: BSD-3-Clause (modified upstream sources)
Base-commit: 07f619c12dd80052f865c51e5d8c77d860c68c64

The current manifest does not request the system shared UID. The existing
user=system rule therefore never selects vendor_timekeep_app, leaving the
platform-signed receiver in platform_app without its RTC and time-adjust
property access.

Select the existing dedicated domain for the package's regular app UID,
with normal application data labeling and per-app MLS categories. Reuse
the existing domain permissions rather than granting them to platform_app.

--- a/sepolicy/vendor/seapp_contexts
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/seapp_contexts
@@ -1 +1 @@
-user=system seinfo=platform name=com.sony.timekeep domain=vendor_timekeep_app
+user=_app seinfo=platform name=com.sony.timekeep domain=vendor_timekeep_app type=app_data_file levelFrom=all
